cross join (values
    ('Rusted metal door handle', 'Look for a handle with reddish-brown rust coating, rough texture, and possibly flaking or pitted metal surface where moisture has eaten away the material.', 'Show a metal door handle with visible rust, oxidation, or discoloration. The rust must appear as orange/brown surface patina or pitting.', 'common'::public.item_rarity, 'Rust (iron oxide) is lighter than the original metal—a corroded door handle has expanded and become more voluminous than before.', 'https://cejsntpvctcgezrluvql.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/collection-item-images/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001/wiki-cache/f6909172aa56da2c.jpg', 0),
    ('Peeling paint layers on wooden door', 'Find areas where multiple paint layers are curling or lifting away from the wood, revealing different colored layers underneath and exposing bare wood.', 'Display a wooden door with paint actively peeling away in flakes or strips, exposing wood underneath or multiple paint colors.', 'common'::public.item_rarity, 'Multiple paint layers on old doors can be radio-dated using lead paint regulations; U.S. residential lead paint bans didn''t occur until 1978.', 'https://cejsntpvctcgezrluvql.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/collection-item-images/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001/wiki-cache/9f0901e2d9166dd2.jpg', 1),
    ('Corroded brass doorknob', 'Search for a doorknob with dull green or blackish patina, discoloration, and rough spots where the shiny brass finish has oxidized away.', 'Show a brass doorknob with visible green patina, tarnish, or corrosion marks covering the surface.', 'common'::public.item_rarity, 'Brass naturally disinfects itself; copper compounds in brass kill 99.9% of bacteria within 4 hours through oxidation reactions.', 'https://cejsntpvctcgezrluvql.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/collection-item-images/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001/wiki-cache/b94c403f5b99bfe5.jpg', 2),
    ('Weathered wood grain texture', 'Look for wood that shows pronounced grain patterns, raised fibers, and a silvery-gray appearance from long exposure to sun and weather.', 'Capture clear wood grain patterns on a door surface that show fading, surface erosion, or natural weathering lines.', 'common'::public.item_rarity, 'UV light permanently breaks wood lignin bonds; weathered wood texture represents actual chemical degradation, not just surface erosion.', 'https://cejsntpvctcgezrluvql.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/collection-item-images/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001/wiki-cache/7c520b8f0eb5cc43.jpg', 3),
    ('Oxidized door hinge', 'Find hinges that have lost their shine, showing dark discoloration, white crusty corrosion deposits, or a mottled color from oxidation.', 'Display a door hinge with rust, oxidation, or tarnish visible on the metal surface and edges.', 'common'::public.item_rarity, 'Iron oxide (rust) has roughly twice the volume of the iron it came from, which is why corroded hinges can seize door mechanisms solid.', 'https://cejsntpvctcgezrluvql.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/collection-item-images/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001/wiki-cache/b7391d582d66d47d.jpg', 4),
    ('Cracked and faded door paint', 'Look for a painted door surface where the color is washed out, with visible cracks spreading across the paint in patterns.', 'Show door paint with visible cracks running across the surface and color fading or discoloration throughout.', 'common'::public.item_rarity, 'Paint cracks follow linear fractal patterns similar to river deltas; stress distribution in weathered coatings creates mathematically predictable crack networks.', 'https://cejsntpvctcgezrluvql.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/collection-item-images/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001/wiki-cache/f07076ab4b64b051.jpg', 5),
    ('Tarnished silver kickplate', 'Search for a metal kickplate at the base of the door that has lost its shine and shows dark spots, patina, or dull gray discoloration.', 'Display a silver or chrome kickplate at the base of a door showing dark tarnish, oxidation, or dull patina.', 'uncommon'::public.item_rarity, 'Tarnish on silver is silver sulfide, not oxidation; it forms through reaction with sulfur compounds in air, not oxygen.', null, 6),
    ('Splintered door frame edge', 'Find the wooden frame edges where wood fibers have split and raised up, creating rough, sharp points and fraying along the corners.', 'Capture the edge of a door frame with visible wood splinters, roughed grain, or splintering damage.', 'uncommon'::public.item_rarity, 'Wood splinters form when weathering exposes grain where fibers align parallel to the surface, creating weak shear points.', null, 7),
    ('Aged copper door knocker', 'Look for a copper knocker with a deep green or brown patina coating that has built up over years of weathering.', 'Show a copper door knocker with visible green or blue patina, tarnish, or age-related color change.', 'uncommon'::public.item_rarity, 'Verdigris (green copper patina) is copper carbonate, which is toxic when ingested but protective—it prevents further copper corrosion underneath.', 'https://cejsntpvctcgezrluvql.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/collection-item-images/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001/wiki-cache/299ddd107084639f.png', 8),
    ('Rust stains bleeding on painted surface', 'Find areas where rust from metal hardware or nails has stained the paint around it, creating orange or reddish streaks and halos.', 'Display a painted door surface with rust-colored stains or streaks running down, showing oxidation bleed-through.', 'uncommon'::public.item_rarity, 'Rust migration stains indicate subsurface iron oxidation continues under paint; the stains track ferric oxide-rich water flowing through cracks.', 'https://cejsntpvctcgezrluvql.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/collection-item-images/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001/wiki-cache/a024a360ad429c93.jpg', 9),
    ('Worn threshold strip', 'Look at the metal or wood strip at the base of the door where foot traffic has created wear patterns, scratches, and a polished or abraded appearance.', 'Show a door threshold strip at the base worn smooth, discolored, or showing significant surface wear and fading.', 'common'::public.item_rarity, 'Door thresholds experience foot traffic compression; metals like brass actually cold-work and harden through repeated impact stress.', 'https://cejsntpvctcgezrluvql.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/collection-item-images/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001/wiki-cache/b4db1b2ee0c74259.jpg', 10),
